00:30:39,560 --> 00:30:41,760
as he showed up.

285
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:45,280
Anyway, an interesting result out of all this reasoning where

286
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:48,640
we just figure that the world is so vast that any one

287
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:51,080
individual can neglect strategy is

288
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:53,280
that once you make the problem simple in this way,

289
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:56,200
thinking that the world does not pay any attention to you,

290
00:30:56,200 --> 00:30:58,840
then you can make the problem complex in every other way

291
00:30:58,840 --> 00:31:01,360
that you can imagine practically.

292
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:04,240
And you can still get clean answers.

293
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:06,240
Now, I say clean answers, not true answers,

294
00:31:06,240 --> 00:31:07,920
but clean answers.

295
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:11,040
If you are, in fact, a theorist, then a lot of what

296
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:13,440
you're looking for is, in fact, a clean answer rather than

297
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:14,680
a true answer, unfortunately.

298
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:15,600
I don't know why.

299
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:18,880
Well, because people can make their career off of, say,

