00:47:18,480 --> 00:47:20,120
and then we're OK.

181
00:47:20,120 --> 00:47:23,520
Then a plus b goes on to 1 again.

182
00:47:23,520 --> 00:47:25,520
And remember, what's the difference

183
00:47:25,520 --> 00:47:27,840
in maximizing utility and maximizing utility divided

184
00:47:27,840 --> 00:47:30,040
by 1.7?

185
00:47:30,040 --> 00:47:31,680
No difference.

186
00:47:31,680 --> 00:47:32,920
There's no difference at all.

187
00:47:32,920 --> 00:47:34,920
What's the difference between maximizing profits

188
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:36,000
and half of profits?

189
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:37,720
It's the same thing.

190
00:47:37,720 --> 00:47:39,640
The way you maximize half of profits

191
00:47:39,640 --> 00:47:41,200
is for maximizing profits.

192
00:47:41,200 --> 00:47:44,840
Same way you maximize twice, you've got two times profits.

193
00:47:44,840 --> 00:47:47,240
Justice aside, this is one of the dumbest arguments

194
00:47:47,240 --> 00:47:51,240
for why excess profit taxation is harmless.

195
00:47:51,240 --> 00:47:53,960
But I have seen economists make a straight face.

196
00:47:53,960 --> 00:47:55,600
Look, it's just calculus.

197
00:47:55,600 --> 00:47:58,560
Excess profit taxation doesn't harm incentives at all

198
00:47:58,560 --> 00:48:02,520
because if people are doing something, maximizing profits,

199
00:48:02,520 --> 00:48:04,800
then we can take half away, and they still

200
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:06,600
do exactly the same thing.

201
00:48:06,600 --> 00:48:08,400
I'll leave you to ponder why this actually

202
00:48:08,400 --> 00:48:09,440
is such a dumb argument.

203
00:48:13,040 --> 00:48:14,480
Back to this.

204
00:48:14,480 --> 00:48:17,040
So then we can go and solve for this whole thing.

205
00:48:17,040 --> 00:48:21,160
And what we will get is Px over Py.

206
00:48:21,160 --> 00:48:24,680
So notice, there aren't any subscripts for individuals

207
00:48:24,680 --> 00:48:26,120
for Px and Py.

208
00:48:26,120 --> 00:48:28,800
Why do the prices not have individual subscripts?

209
00:48:31,800 --> 00:48:34,920
Because there's no price discrimination.

210
00:48:34,920 --> 00:48:38,320
Because this is a market.

211
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:40,560
This is a market where each individual is not

212
00:48:40,560 --> 00:48:41,920
