27
01:61:03,840 --> 01:61:06,040
Now, generally, it starts out seeming pretty general,

28
01:61:06,040 --> 01:61:08,440
good for any number of agents, any number of goods.

29
01:61:08,440 --> 01:61:09,440
All right.

30
01:61:09,440 --> 01:61:11,080
But then Errod De Broglie said, wait a second,

31
01:61:11,080 --> 01:61:14,600
this is actually way more general than it seems at first.

32
01:61:14,600 --> 01:61:15,440
Why?

33
01:61:15,440 --> 01:61:16,280
Well, he said, first of all,

34
01:61:16,280 --> 01:61:18,600
our theorem can actually be extended immediately

35
01:61:18,600 --> 01:61:20,400
to intertemporal markets.

36
01:61:20,400 --> 01:61:21,240
Why?

37
01:61:21,240 --> 01:61:24,600
So, just think of good trading at time t

38
01:61:24,600 --> 01:61:25,840
as being a different good

39
01:61:25,840 --> 01:61:28,560
than good k trading at time t plus y.

40
01:61:28,560 --> 01:61:30,080
And then basically, we say,

41
01:61:30,080 --> 01:61:32,840
well, instead of having k physical goods,

42
01:61:32,840 --> 01:61:37,120
we can have k times t intertemporal goods.

43
01:61:38,800 --> 01:61:41,520
All right, and then we just go and redefine k.

44
01:61:41,520 --> 01:61:44,320
I'll explain what it is, I'll take new k

45
01:61:44,320 --> 01:61:47,600
is gonna be equal to old k times t, the number of periods.

46
01:61:47,600 --> 01:61:49,800
And now we've got a model that actually allows

47
01:61:49,800 --> 01:61:52,080
for an arbitrary amount of intertemporal trade.

48
01:61:52,080 --> 01:61:56,280
So, now I could go and trade bananas in 2019

49
01:61:56,280 --> 01:61:59,560
for driverless cars in 2037.

50
01:61:59,560 --> 01:62:01,720
And we could go and write a contract about that.

51
01:62:01,720 --> 01:62:02,960
We can exchange that,

52
01:62:02,960 --> 01:62:05,120
and that could be a perfectly competitive market

53
01:62:05,120 --> 01:62:07,400
where we go and exchange pieces of paper

54
01:62:07,400 --> 01:62:09,200
for goods that don't even exist yet.

55
01:62:10,640 --> 01:62:12,120
That would be possible.

56
01:62:12,120 --> 01:62:13,880
All right, so instead of trading current goods,

57
01:62:13,880 --> 01:62:15,040
instead of it being a bargain market

58
01:62:15,040 --> 01:62:17,640
where I hand you bananas now for cars now,

59
01:62:17,640 --> 01:62:20,840
I'm handing pieces of paper which are just promissory notes.

60
01:62:20,840 --> 01:62:23,160
And we can have a giant market in these promissory notes

61
01:62:23,160 --> 01:62:24,680
where every conceivable promissory note

62
01:62:24,680 --> 01:62:27,560
